    delphi:hasConfidence "0.73"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The statistic is straightforward, but datasets linking pedigrees to repeated age-specific traits are scattered and biased toward disease. Only limited domains can be tested now." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In pedigrees with longitudinal phenotyping, compare age of onset of a heritable trait in parents and offspring against shuffled parent-offspring pairs. Positive age concordance supports the rule; no concordance refutes it." ;
